WEBVTT

00:14.680 --> 00:17.640
My weapon is my magnificent shooting technique!

00:17.720 --> 00:20.060
With the slogan "Sexy Football!"

00:20.140 --> 00:21.850
I'm good at sneaking behind the defense.

00:21.930 --> 00:24.940
Mine is physical ability.

00:25.020 --> 00:26.980
Being versatile, I guess.

00:27.060 --> 00:28.610
Mine is never giving up!

00:28.690 --> 00:30.570
Powerful left-footed shots.

00:30.650 --> 00:32.280
Mine is speed and technique.

00:33.320 --> 00:35.240
Dribbling.

00:35.320 --> 00:36.660
"Dribbling."

00:37.240 --> 00:38.740
I'm good at jumping.

00:38.830 --> 00:41.000
You're next, Isagi-kun.

00:41.080 --> 00:42.290
My weapon?

00:43.000 --> 00:45.750
Ah, what could it be?

00:45.830 --> 00:46.960
Maybe your passes?

00:47.040 --> 00:49.550
As a forward, I can't say that.

00:49.630 --> 00:53.050
If you don't even know your weapon, you're useless. Next.

00:53.130 --> 00:54.340
Wait, hold on.

00:54.430 --> 00:57.010
Then tell us when you think of it.

00:57.090 --> 00:58.680
Lastly, Chigiri.

01:00.100 --> 01:01.140
I'm not saying.

01:02.220 --> 01:05.390
We agreed at the start that we'd all share our weapons.

01:06.150 --> 01:08.650
I know, but I'm still not saying.

01:08.730 --> 01:12.650
What's with her? Forget that selfish queen.

01:12.740 --> 01:14.530
Nothing we can do.

01:14.610 --> 01:17.870
Anyway, I think a forward needs a powerful weapon,

01:17.950 --> 01:20.750
and knowing how to use it is crucial.

01:20.780 --> 01:24.620
But if everyone just does what they want, won't it turn into the same mess as last game?

01:25.210 --> 01:29.210
Can we really win by following what Ego said?

01:29.290 --> 01:30.840
Even if we have weapons,

01:30.920 --> 01:32.870
it's meaningless if we can't become a team.

01:34.170 --> 01:38.220
Can't we think of a method where each of us shines?

01:41.010 --> 01:42.060
I get it now.

01:42.850 --> 01:46.310
This could work. And everyone gets an equal chance.

01:47.020 --> 01:49.480
We can win with this plan.

01:50.060 --> 01:51.070
Its name is

01:51.730 --> 01:54.030
the 'Next 11 is Me' plan!

01:58.490 --> 01:59.490
<i>What a terrible name.</i>

03:31.000 --> 03:35.000
CHAPTER 4: FORESIGHT AND INTUITION

03:37.130 --> 03:38.760
Pass the ball with this timing.

03:38.840 --> 03:39.840
Got it!

03:41.220 --> 03:44.430
<i>I can't say we instantly became a team, but...</i>

03:44.510 --> 03:47.680
Not like that, a bit more towards my feet.

03:47.770 --> 03:49.770
Shut up, we got it already!

03:49.850 --> 03:51.190
Isagi, don't drop back!

03:51.270 --> 03:52.100
Hold the line!

03:52.190 --> 03:53.310
Okay.

03:53.400 --> 03:55.690
<i>If we lose, our careers are over.</i>

03:56.360 --> 04:01.990
<i>I feel like only that harsh reality is bringing us together.</i>

04:05.910 --> 04:07.620
NATTO

04:10.330 --> 04:12.710
I'm way too late.

04:15.420 --> 04:17.960
<i>It's been a week since I came here.</i>

04:18.050 --> 04:21.550
<i>To be honest, my confidence is completely shattered.</i>

04:22.340 --> 04:25.720
<i>I don't have a weapon I can boast about.</i>

04:26.260 --> 04:29.180
"You're just talentless."

04:32.850 --> 04:36.310
<i>Maybe I really don't have any talent.</i>

04:42.150 --> 04:44.070
I'm sick of natto already.

04:44.150 --> 04:45.320
Well done, Isagi.

04:46.120 --> 04:47.120
Kunigami.

04:48.280 --> 04:50.290
Do you always get natto?

04:51.790 --> 04:53.500
That's what they give to low-ranked players.

04:54.120 --> 04:56.250
Wait, you still haven't eaten your meal?

04:56.330 --> 04:57.380
I ate just a bit ago.

04:58.170 --> 04:59.710
I came to talk to you.

04:59.800 --> 05:00.920
About what?

05:01.880 --> 05:05.260
I realized I still haven't said it to you.

05:05.340 --> 05:06.180
What?

05:07.340 --> 05:09.050
Thanks for the pass.

05:10.850 --> 05:14.100
Ah, from that game. Did you come all this way just to say that?

05:14.180 --> 05:18.110
Yeah. After all, doing things properly is my motto.

05:18.190 --> 05:20.520
Anyway, that was all. Goodnight.

05:20.610 --> 05:21.730
Hey, wait.

05:23.440 --> 05:26.700
Why do you play soccer, Kunigami?

05:27.740 --> 05:29.160
What kind of question is that?

05:29.240 --> 05:31.330
Uh, nothing.

05:31.410 --> 05:34.370
You've got the physique, the shot power,

05:34.870 --> 05:37.500
a bunch of weapons I don't have.

05:37.580 --> 05:39.750
I just wondered what someone as amazing as you

05:39.840 --> 05:42.250
thinks about.

05:42.340 --> 05:45.010
Ah, forget it, what am I even saying?

05:45.090 --> 05:48.510
Sorry, now that I think about it, it's super embarrassing.

05:48.590 --> 05:50.890
Pretend I didn't ask. Goodnight.

05:50.970 --> 05:52.600
The answer's simple.

05:53.520 --> 05:56.600
I'm going to become a superhero of soccer.

05:56.690 --> 05:57.690
What?

05:58.100 --> 06:04.900
When I was little, I didn't admire <i>Sentai</i> heroes, robots, or pirate kings.

06:07.240 --> 06:12.280
<i>I only admired forwards running on green fields, scoring goals for victory.</i>

06:12.370 --> 06:13.830
<i></i>

06:15.250 --> 06:17.460
<i>Those warriors, completely real,</i>

06:18.040 --> 06:22.590
<i>were real-life superheroes that gave me excitement and courage.</i>

06:24.420 --> 06:27.010
I want to be like them.

06:28.300 --> 06:30.430
You're serious, I guess.

06:30.510 --> 06:35.470
Of course. Even if they call me stupid and laugh at me, I don't care.

06:36.140 --> 06:38.520
There's nothing to be ashamed of in my dream.

06:38.600 --> 06:43.110
I will honestly hold my head high to the world for my dreams.

06:43.770 --> 06:44.770
<i>Man,</i>

06:45.530 --> 06:49.490
<i>this guy has a determination I don't possess.</i>

06:51.280 --> 06:52.280
Not bad.

06:52.950 --> 06:54.330
You're pretty damn cool.

06:58.040 --> 07:00.170
Isagi, want to eat together?

07:01.210 --> 07:02.960
What, steak?

07:03.040 --> 07:03.880
How?

07:03.960 --> 07:05.590
BL RANK 274
MENU: NATTO

07:05.670 --> 07:08.170
The goal bonus written over there.

07:08.260 --> 07:12.890
It looks like a system where you can get rewards with points if you score goals.

07:12.970 --> 07:16.010
<i>A cell phone? A bed? I want those too!</i>

07:16.100 --> 07:17.890
<i>A day-off pass?</i>

07:17.980 --> 07:21.480
Half of that goal was thanks to you.

07:22.230 --> 07:24.190
So half of this steak is yours too.

07:24.270 --> 07:26.110
What, are you sure about this?

07:26.190 --> 07:29.280
Meat, after so long! I'm freed from natto!

07:29.900 --> 07:33.450
By the way, why did you pass to me in that moment?

07:35.080 --> 07:37.450
<i>Raichi was clearly more open,</i>

07:37.540 --> 07:42.830
I'm curious why you deliberately passed to me when I was marked.

07:42.920 --> 07:45.840
I moved unconsciously at that moment.

07:45.920 --> 07:47.630
It was like a reflex.

07:47.710 --> 07:50.050
Even if I had passed to Raichi, probably

07:50.130 --> 07:52.550
we still would have had Barou against us.

07:52.630 --> 07:57.060
Instead, from your mid-range shot, I smelled a goal.

07:57.140 --> 07:59.930
<i>I had experienced it before, after all.</i>

08:00.520 --> 08:01.770
Smelled a goal?

08:02.690 --> 08:05.650
Could that be your weapon?

08:06.440 --> 08:10.740
Making such a split-second decision in that moment is an incredible talent.

08:13.030 --> 08:15.280
Ah! So delicious!

08:15.370 --> 08:16.910
Eat it quickly, Isagi.

08:16.990 --> 08:18.080
Okay.

08:19.790 --> 08:22.660
Incredibly delicious!

08:23.330 --> 08:24.370
Right?

08:24.460 --> 08:28.050
Thanks, Kunigami. Thanks to you, my spirits are back.

08:28.130 --> 08:30.260
You're really a good guy.

08:31.800 --> 08:34.590
Shut up, I'm not that good.

08:36.180 --> 08:39.350
Oh, are you the type who gets embarrassed when praised?

08:39.430 --> 08:42.520
Ugh, whatever. After we eat, we're going to bed.

08:42.600 --> 08:44.190
And in the next match,

08:46.150 --> 08:47.940
we'll definitely win.

08:51.860 --> 08:52.860
Hell yeah!

08:55.280 --> 08:58.240
BLUE LOCK
BUILDING 5 - MATCH 4

09:00.330 --> 09:01.330
They're here.

09:02.830 --> 09:03.830
Team Y.

09:05.370 --> 09:09.670
Just like us, Team Y lost their first match and are on the brink.

09:09.750 --> 09:11.130
They won't hold back.

09:11.760 --> 09:14.010
We need to watch out for their number 9.

09:14.630 --> 09:16.640
He's got an unusual shooting technique.

09:16.720 --> 09:18.350
The top scorer of Kumamoto Prefecture.

09:18.350 --> 09:22.850
BL RANK 254
OKAWA HIBIKI

09:18.930 --> 09:20.350
Okawa Hibiki.

09:20.430 --> 09:21.850
Let's go, guys!

09:21.930 --> 09:22.930
Okay!

09:24.140 --> 09:27.440
But this time, we have a plan.

09:27.520 --> 09:29.650
Our efforts will pay off.

09:29.730 --> 09:32.110
We'll win even if it kills us, Team Z!

09:32.190 --> 09:33.240
Okay!

09:34.280 --> 09:35.320
Here we go.

09:35.400 --> 09:38.410
<i>The key to our plan is the weapons Ego mentioned.</i>

09:39.070 --> 09:41.410
So that everyone can use their weapons,

09:41.490 --> 09:43.160
we're implementing this extremely aggressive plan.

09:43.250 --> 09:46.210
But if everyone uses their weapon randomly,

09:46.290 --> 09:47.620
we'll fall apart.

09:48.630 --> 09:50.920
<i>We'll divide the time equally and ensure</i>

09:50.950 --> 09:53.130
<i>that everyone plays as forward in turn.</i>

09:53.210 --> 09:57.880
<i>To highlight one person's weapon, the rest will adapt and</i>

09:57.970 --> 10:00.850
<i>support them in the way they want to play.</i>

10:00.930 --> 10:03.140
Equal time for everyone sounds nice, but

10:03.220 --> 10:04.370
how do we decide the order?

10:04.430 --> 10:06.440
Can't we just go by our rankings?

10:06.520 --> 10:08.600
What about the positions other than forward?

10:08.690 --> 10:11.360
Constantly changing positions will confuse us.

10:11.440 --> 10:15.440
If everyone shifts one position clockwise, there's no problem.

10:15.530 --> 10:18.110
Since the distances are short, it won't be an issue.

10:18.200 --> 10:20.820
But if the goalkeeper keeps changing among 11 people,

10:20.910 --> 10:23.910
it's very risky defensively.

10:24.830 --> 10:28.040
I can accept being goalkeeper in order to win.

10:28.120 --> 10:30.170
I can also stay in defense.

10:31.170 --> 10:35.210
Since you're staying in the background like that, you must be talentless!

10:35.300 --> 10:37.510
So, even though I'm not thrilled about it,

10:37.590 --> 10:40.640
I'll go along with your plan just this once.

10:40.720 --> 10:42.470
Me too.

10:42.550 --> 10:45.360
Alright, if we exclude Chigiri and Iemon,

10:45.390 --> 10:48.940
everyone will change positions every 10 minutes.

10:49.020 --> 10:51.100
<i>The name 'Next 11 is Me',</i>

10:55.730 --> 10:56.940
Let's go!

10:56.440 --> 10:58.000
BL RANK 265
BACHIRA MEGURU

10:57.030 --> 10:59.200
<i>we're changing it to 'Next 9 is Me'.</i>

11:01.530 --> 11:03.410
<i>Bachira's weapon is dribbling.</i>

11:03.490 --> 11:06.660
<i>A one-man tactic where he goes as far as he can.</i>

11:07.500 --> 11:12.580
<i>An egoistic tactic meant only for those with irresistible weapons.</i>

11:12.670 --> 11:13.790
Two-man mark him!

11:13.880 --> 11:15.590
Don't let him advance further!

11:15.670 --> 11:16.710
Is two enough?

11:16.800 --> 11:18.300
I'll slip right through.

11:19.420 --> 11:23.430
We're three. I've thoroughly studied your dribbling style.

11:23.510 --> 11:25.310
You're not bad, Mr. Bangs.

11:25.390 --> 11:26.930
In that case, I'll play it back.

11:27.020 --> 11:28.020
Got it!

11:29.060 --> 11:34.060
<i>They tried to block him with two and trap him with the third.</i>

11:34.150 --> 11:35.690
Keep an eye on number 8 too!

11:35.770 --> 11:36.610
Okay!

11:36.690 --> 11:38.820
<i>-This isn't improvisation.</i>
-Number 9 is coming, mark him!

11:38.900 --> 11:40.990
<i>They have a plan too.</i>

11:41.070 --> 11:42.740
<i>Of course they do.</i>

11:42.820 --> 11:44.780
<i>It's their last chance too.</i>

11:44.870 --> 11:46.410
-Bachira, one more time!
-Okay.

11:46.490 --> 11:47.450
Coming from the wing!

11:47.540 --> 11:48.950
Don't leave any openings!

11:49.040 --> 11:53.250
<i>Against our aggressive plan to use our weapons,</i>

11:53.330 --> 11:56.380
<i>they're playing to stop our weapons.</i>

11:56.460 --> 11:58.920
<i>Bachira's dribbling is definitely working.</i>

11:59.000 --> 12:02.710
<i>On top of that, we have 8 more weapons.</i>

12:02.760 --> 12:05.210
<i>If we keep pressing like this, we'll surely find an opening.</i>

12:05.440 --> 12:06.390
<i>We can win!</i>

12:06.690 --> 12:07.760
Hey, 10 minutes are up!

12:07.850 --> 12:08.930
Okay.

12:09.720 --> 12:10.730
Wings, spread out!

12:10.200 --> 12:11.690
BL RANK 266
KUNIGAMI RENSUKE

12:13.940 --> 12:16.690
<i>Kunigami's weapon is his mid-range left-footed shots.</i>

12:16.770 --> 12:18.820
<i>He'll run straight towards the opponent's goal,</i>

12:18.900 --> 12:22.070
<i>just outside the crowded penalty area,</i>

12:22.150 --> 12:23.740
Just like we practiced!

12:23.820 --> 12:24.910
<i>receive the ball,</i>

12:24.990 --> 12:26.660
-Shoot!
-You can do it now!

12:26.740 --> 12:29.540
<i>and shoot through the opening we created!</i>

12:31.790 --> 12:33.500
<i>Did they block his shot?</i>

12:33.580 --> 12:35.460
Whoop, out of bounds!

12:35.540 --> 12:37.670
<i>Their defense is really solid.</i>

12:41.800 --> 12:43.470
Bachira, let's rebuild the play.

12:43.550 --> 12:44.760
Got it.

12:44.840 --> 12:46.850
Close the gaps in front of number 9.

12:46.930 --> 12:47.890
Double-team him!

12:47.930 --> 12:50.810
<i>More than that, they're not attacking at all.</i>

12:51.390 --> 12:54.060
<i>And Okawa hasn't done anything either.</i>

12:54.980 --> 12:57.770
<i>He's the only one not going back to defend, is he waiting for something?</i>

12:59.520 --> 13:00.730
Nice pass, Bachira.

13:00.820 --> 13:02.070
I'll shoot this time!

13:03.900 --> 13:05.410
Damn, again!

13:05.490 --> 13:06.950
Get the loose ball!

13:13.830 --> 13:16.460
<i>Shit, was this their plan?</i>

13:16.540 --> 13:19.590
That's right, I was waiting for this moment.

13:20.300 --> 13:22.260
<i>We weren't pressuring them.</i>

13:22.340 --> 13:24.050
<i>They made us think that!</i>

13:24.130 --> 13:25.630
<i>Their goal is,</i>

13:26.220 --> 13:27.970
So you finally pass it, Niko.

13:28.930 --> 13:30.310
Thanks to you,

13:30.310 --> 13:31.930
BL RANK 255
NIKO IKKI

13:30.390 --> 13:31.930
Okawa.

13:32.020 --> 13:33.520
<i>a counter-attack!</i>

13:42.440 --> 13:43.530
<i>We were tricked.</i>

13:43.610 --> 13:46.070
<i>Their target is Kumamoto's top scorer,</i>

13:47.240 --> 13:48.240
<i>Okawa!</i>

13:49.530 --> 13:50.660
<i>He's coming!</i>

14:02.920 --> 14:04.550
-Nice!
-Great shot!

14:04.630 --> 14:05.720
That's just the first!

14:07.130 --> 14:12.720
<i>They were looking for an opportunity to use Okawa Hibiki's superior shooting technique.</i>

14:12.810 --> 14:15.430
<i></i>

14:15.520 --> 14:19.600
Weren't you supposed to be marking him, Naruhaya? Don't leave Okawa free!

14:19.690 --> 14:21.730
I can't stop him alone!

14:21.820 --> 14:23.650
We need two people!

14:23.730 --> 14:25.740
<i>Now everything makes sense.</i>

14:25.820 --> 14:30.370
<i>Their plan is to fall back, wait for an opening, and then counter-attack.</i>

14:30.450 --> 14:34.080
<i>If we can't stop Okawa, we have no chance of winning.</i>

14:34.160 --> 14:35.580
Let's score another one!

14:36.500 --> 14:39.500
Pull yourselves together. It's only one goal.

14:39.580 --> 14:42.210
<i>He's right. We still have time.</i>

14:42.290 --> 14:43.630
Leave the rest to you, Kuon!

14:43.710 --> 14:45.630
<i>Kuon's weapon is jumping.</i>

14:46.720 --> 14:49.550
BL RANK 268
KUON WATARU

14:47.600 --> 14:51.550
<i>He claims the ball in the air and quickly passes it to a nearby teammate to start the attack.</i>

14:51.720 --> 14:53.970
-Surround him!
-Double-team him!

14:54.060 --> 14:55.850
<i>God dammit, they're throwing obstacles in my way.</i>

14:55.930 --> 14:57.890
Your feet have stopped.

14:57.980 --> 14:59.190
<i>It's coming!</i>

15:01.730 --> 15:03.570
<i>Are they passing around in their own half?</i>

15:03.650 --> 15:04.520
<i>Oh, right.</i>

15:04.610 --> 15:06.990
<i>Since they're ahead, they don't need to attack.</i>

15:15.370 --> 15:17.160
<i>They're trying to run out the clock.</i>

15:17.750 --> 15:19.250
<i>This is bad.</i>

15:20.540 --> 15:23.380
That's it! Raichi's time has come!

15:20.550 --> 15:24.580
BL RANK 269
RAICHI JINGO

15:23.400 --> 15:25.490
Pass every ball that comes to you to me.

15:25.500 --> 15:28.380
I'll handle the rest somehow.

15:28.470 --> 15:29.670
TIME UNTIL HALF-TIME

15:31.200 --> 15:33.960
Are you guys messing with me? Get that ball already!

15:34.010 --> 15:37.060
In my 10-minute period, the ball was always with the opponent.

15:37.140 --> 15:39.350
My first 5 minutes were the same.

15:39.430 --> 15:41.390
It ended without doing a damn thing.

15:41.480 --> 15:43.100
Even if you say that,

15:43.100 --> 15:46.360
if we push too hard trying to get the ball, what if they pass to Okawa?

15:47.070 --> 15:48.690
At this rate, we'll lose!

15:48.780 --> 15:50.950
Is your brain working, moron? If we lose, it's over.

15:51.030 --> 15:53.910
But if we concede one more goal, we can't overturn the match no matter what.

15:53.990 --> 15:54.950
Think a little!

15:56.200 --> 15:57.950
Don't fight among yourselves.

15:58.040 --> 16:01.330
Even professional players struggle

16:01.350 --> 16:04.040
to break down teams that park the bus like this.

16:04.130 --> 16:07.000
If we don't play more aggressively in the second half, we can't win.

16:07.090 --> 16:10.130
More importantly, do you think this plan will work?

16:10.220 --> 16:14.720
As long as our weapons aren't functioning, losing is only a matter of time.

16:14.750 --> 16:18.760
Why is someone who can't even swallow their pride and reveal their weapon complaining?

16:18.770 --> 16:20.730
To increase our chances of winning,

16:20.810 --> 16:23.400
instead of wasting time with unusable weapons,

16:23.480 --> 16:27.360
we should focus on those like Bachira and Kunigami

16:27.410 --> 16:28.990
who disrupt the opponent's order.

16:29.030 --> 16:31.570
Who's the "unusable" one, huh?!

16:31.650 --> 16:33.070
Don't argue.

16:33.150 --> 16:35.920
Changing our plan now would be too risky.

16:35.950 --> 16:39.200
Instead, continuing to change our tactics

16:39.290 --> 16:42.120
will prevent the opponent from taking measures against us.

16:42.210 --> 16:44.120
Our attacks are working.

16:44.540 --> 16:46.310
Without fearing Okawa's counters,

16:46.330 --> 16:47.960
let's all attack together!

16:48.040 --> 16:50.260
Continue the 'Next 9 is Me' plan!

16:50.340 --> 16:52.050
This is our best option!

16:52.130 --> 16:52.970
-Okay!
-Understood!

16:56.970 --> 16:59.890
<i>Can we really win like this?</i>

17:02.310 --> 17:04.190
SECOND HALF BEGINS

17:04.270 --> 17:05.980
Pass it back! Don't push your luck!

17:06.060 --> 17:07.480
Get the guys running!

17:08.440 --> 17:10.690
This is no different from the first half!

17:10.780 --> 17:13.780
<i>Damn it, even though it's my time,</i>

17:11.500 --> 17:14.300
BL RANK 270
IMAMURA YUDAI

17:13.860 --> 17:15.570
<i>we can't get the ball back.</i>

17:15.660 --> 17:17.740
<i>If I pressure them, they'll break away,</i>

17:17.820 --> 17:20.700
<i>but waiting won't change anything either.</i>

17:20.790 --> 17:23.790
<i>For me, soccer is no different from romance!</i>

17:23.870 --> 17:26.540
<i>This situation is exactly like a girl</i>

17:26.620 --> 17:28.170
<i>being out of your league!</i>

17:28.250 --> 17:29.420
<i>Even though it seems tough at first,</i>

17:29.500 --> 17:32.380
<i>she's actually a type with zero experience in love,</i>

17:32.460 --> 17:35.010
<i>but once I get her, she'll fall head over heels.</i>

17:35.090 --> 17:37.510
<i>That's exactly Team Y-chan!</i>

17:37.590 --> 17:40.430
<i>Just once is enough. After that, Miss Y is an easy target.</i>

17:40.510 --> 17:41.720
I stole it!

17:41.810 --> 17:43.060
Come on already!

17:43.140 --> 17:46.480
Our pressing wasn't in vain.

17:47.190 --> 17:48.650
10 minutes are up!

17:48.730 --> 17:50.520
My turn.

17:49.610 --> 17:51.610
BL RANK 271
GAGAMARU GIN

17:51.690 --> 17:53.440
We finally got the ball!

17:53.530 --> 17:55.860
Change positions! Gagamaru formation!

17:56.450 --> 17:59.570
<i>7th minute of the second half. It's the perfect time to score.</i>

17:59.660 --> 18:01.530
-Leaving it to you, Isagi.
-Okay!

18:02.240 --> 18:05.000
<i>Gagamaru's plan starts with me on the wing.</i>

18:05.080 --> 18:06.920
<i>The goal is an early cross</i>

18:07.000 --> 18:10.090
<i>to a hard-to-reach spot in front of the goal.</i>

18:11.130 --> 18:12.800
<i>Damn, I kicked it too far.</i>

18:14.710 --> 18:18.090
<i>I'm sure he can reach it; his weapon is physical ability.</i>

18:21.510 --> 18:22.760
So close!

18:22.840 --> 18:24.650
We can still do this! Take the corner!

18:24.680 --> 18:26.230
How did he reach that ball?

18:26.310 --> 18:27.440
Corner coming!

18:27.520 --> 18:29.060
I'll try again.

18:29.810 --> 18:33.360
<i>Great, this weapon is working. We can do this!</i>

18:37.200 --> 18:39.360
<i>What was that just now?</i>

18:39.450 --> 18:40.570
<i>Was that Okawa?</i>

18:41.160 --> 18:46.540
<i>If we don't capitalize on this chance, it could turn into a counter-attack.</i>

18:46.620 --> 18:48.250
Don't zone out, Isagi!

18:48.330 --> 18:50.170
It's our corner! Get in position!

18:51.710 --> 18:53.210
Fill the goal area!

18:53.290 --> 18:55.130
Just score, the rest doesn't matter!

18:55.760 --> 18:56.880
<i>He's right.</i>

18:56.970 --> 18:59.130
<i>If we don't attack now, when will we?</i>

18:59.220 --> 19:01.390
<i>This is the first real chance we've gotten.</i>

19:02.300 --> 19:04.470
<i>Our first chance.</i>

19:04.560 --> 19:06.350
Now I understand.

19:07.310 --> 19:09.020
<i>The reason for this feeling inside me...</i>

19:09.850 --> 19:10.730
Isagi.

19:10.810 --> 19:11.810
I'm there!

19:12.310 --> 19:14.270
<i>We misunderstood the situation.</i>

19:14.360 --> 19:17.070
<i>The one blocking our chances,</i>

19:17.150 --> 19:22.700
<i>the one pulling the strings and feeding critical passes to Okawa,</i>

19:23.680 --> 19:24.890
-Come on!
-Nice, goalie!

19:24.950 --> 19:25.790
Counter-attack!

19:25.870 --> 19:29.250
Crap, too many of us pushed forward!

19:29.330 --> 19:31.500
If the ball reaches Okawa...

19:37.050 --> 19:38.050
<i>Right there!</i>

19:38.760 --> 19:41.220
<i>The source of that bad feeling inside me,</i>

19:41.300 --> 19:43.180
<i>the heart of Team Y,</i>

19:43.800 --> 19:45.260
<i>is you, Niko!</i>

19:46.890 --> 19:48.020
Well done, Isagi!

19:48.640 --> 19:50.940
<i>If we stop him, Team Y is finished.</i>

19:51.020 --> 19:52.980
<i>The real opportunity is now!</i>

19:57.280 --> 19:59.150
<i>I can shoot now!</i>

20:03.360 --> 20:04.240
<i>Damn it!</i>

20:04.320 --> 20:05.320
<i>I missed.</i>

20:11.830 --> 20:13.330
Yes!

20:13.420 --> 20:16.880
That's it! We got it!

20:18.460 --> 20:20.340
Nice pass, Isagi.

20:20.420 --> 20:21.630
Gagamaru.

20:21.720 --> 20:23.550
<i>Actually, that was a shot, but whatever.</i>

20:23.640 --> 20:25.350
We tied it up!

20:26.180 --> 20:28.100
<i>Ah, I'm celebrating someone else's goal.</i>

20:28.180 --> 20:29.810
So it's even now, right?

20:29.890 --> 20:31.680
You really got there in time!

20:31.770 --> 20:33.140
Gagamaru, you're amazing!

20:33.230 --> 20:36.360
One more goal and we're ahead.

20:36.440 --> 20:37.440
Hell yeah!

20:38.520 --> 20:40.400
I guess I've been found out.

20:40.490 --> 20:45.410
If it weren't for you, I would have ended the match with that counter.

20:45.490 --> 20:47.490
I won't let you do as you please.

20:47.580 --> 20:50.250
I'll stop you and we'll win!

20:54.830 --> 20:57.210
Your eyes are the same as mine.

20:58.130 --> 21:00.260
But you can't beat me.

21:01.880 --> 21:04.720
I'm the one controlling the game.

21:05.720 --> 21:08.260
<i>Wait and see, you bang-haired brat.</i>

22:40.860 --> 22:43.320
<i>Blue Lock, Extra Time.</i>

22:43.980 --> 22:47.990
Hey, what kind of food do you think the others are eating?

22:48.070 --> 22:50.660
I'm sure it's better than natto and pickled radish.

22:51.450 --> 22:52.780
Let's investigate!

22:52.870 --> 22:55.870
What? I'm eating stir-fried vegetables.

22:55.950 --> 22:58.040
An irresistible perfect balance!

22:58.120 --> 22:59.790
I'm incredibly jealous!

23:00.330 --> 23:01.830
Mine is curry.

23:01.920 --> 23:05.630
Are you a king? The best food to go with rice!

23:05.710 --> 23:07.590
Namaste!

23:07.670 --> 23:10.840
Hey Kunigami, do you want to trade?

23:10.930 --> 23:13.720
We'll give you both natto and pickled radish!

23:13.810 --> 23:15.600
Please, just this once!

23:15.680 --> 23:18.480
Let us also taste the curry-sama!

23:18.560 --> 23:20.900
It can't be helped.

23:20.970 --> 23:22.270
Only for today, okay?

23:22.360 --> 23:23.980
Thank you, god!

23:24.070 --> 23:26.530
Curry god, Kunigami-sama!

23:27.570 --> 23:29.320
I want to eat curry too.

23:29.900 --> 23:31.450
Let's trade, Kunigami.

23:32.200 --> 23:34.910
Will you choose these fresh veggies or theirs?

23:36.120 --> 23:37.950
I'm honored you'd choose me!

23:38.040 --> 23:40.500
TRADE COMPLETED

23:40.580 --> 23:42.500
I knew it would turn out like this!

23:42.580 --> 23:44.040
Namaste!